t and Barringer raised over $1 million", "No public general-election polling to confirm the margin"], "rationale": "The district's R+8 lean, Knott's incumbency, and a near-unanimous expert consensus toward Republicans anchor the forecast firmly on the R side. Democratic interest is real — Barringer's fundraising and the DCCC's targeting justify a modest nudge toward the Democrat — but nothing in the evidence suggests a genuine tossup.", "watch": "Any credible general-election polling showing Knott under single digits, or a major outside-spending surge for Barringer, would move this toward Lean R.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Brad Knott (R) is running."]}, "overview": "North Carolina's 13th District leans Republican by about eight points, and first-term incumbent Brad Knott is seeking reelection with roughly $700,000 on hand. Ten expert raters split between Safe R and Likely R, and prediction markets give the Democrat only about a one-in-seven chance. No public general-election polls are available, so the forecast rests on fundamentals and ratings.\n\nThe Democratic side shows unusual energy for a seat this red: Paul Barringer has raised over $1 million, and national Democrats have added the district to their target list amid reporting on softening Trump approval in red North Carolina districts. Still, the structural lean and incumbent advantage point to a Knott win, with Barringer needing a strong national environment to close the gap.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0835, "margin": -8.64}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0743, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1064, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1381, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0942, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0796, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0989, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-2